## 3. Chemical & physical properties; analytics; MSDS
Chemical identity
- Name: Levulinic acid (4‑oxopentanoic acid)  
- CAS: 123‑76‑2  
- PubChem CID: 6137  
- Formula: C5H8O3; MW: 116.12 g·mol‑1

Physical properties (typical values)
- Appearance: colorless to slightly yellow liquid  
- Density: ≈ 1.13 g·cm‑3 (25 °C)  
- Melting point: ≈ −45 °C  
- Boiling point: ≈ 245–246 °C (760 mmHg)  
- pKa: ≈ 4.59  
- Solubility: miscible with polar organics; soluble in water

Analytical methods
- HPLC (UV or RI) for LA and formic acid quantification.  
- GC‑MS (after derivatization) for volatile derivatives and by‑products.  
- 1H/13C NMR for structure/purity confirmation.  
- IR (C=O stretch) and titration for acidity.

MSDS highlights (summary only — consult supplier SDS before work)
- Typical hazard statements: H302 (harmful if swallowed), H315 (causes skin irritation), H319/H318 (causes serious eye irritation/damage), H317 (may cause allergic skin reaction in some SDS variants).  
- Precautions: use chemical‑resistant gloves, eye protection and lab coat; use in fume hood or enclosed systems for pilot; avoid ingestion/inhalation.  
- First aid: flush eyes with water; wash skin; if swallowed, rinse mouth and seek medical attention.  
- Storage/disposal: store cool, dry; avoid incompatible materials (strong oxidizers). Dispose via licensed hazardous waste procedures; neutralize acidic effluents and treat for COD before discharge.

