## 7. Safety, environmental and regulatory considerations
- Use closed systems and vapor recovery to minimize solvent emissions. Ensure proper relief systems for high‑temp/pressurized units and emergency shutdown instrumentation.
- Materials: stainless steel (316L) or lined vessels for hydrothermal conditions; evaluate compatibility with solvent (GVL) and any residual acidity.
- Waste management: neutralize acidic aqueous streams before biological treatment; treat COD/BOD to regulatory levels. Humin solids can be combusted for energy (after testing) or stabilized and disposed in accordance with regulations.
- Personnel safety: PPE (gloves, goggles, lab coat), training on high‑T/P operations, solvent handling and emergency response.
- Permits: environmental clearances for wastewater discharge, air emissions; local factory/industrial permits for pilot plant.

